# chimerax-vampnet tutorial: full v0.1 walkthrough on the chignolin
# CLN025 1 us trajectory.
#
# Prereqs:
#   - chimerax-vampnet bundle installed (toolshed install . from this dir)
#   - chignolin trajectory at /data/datasets/chimerax-vampnet/chignolin_modal/
#     containing replica_0/traj.dcd + equilibrated.pdb
#
# Run inside ChimeraX:
#   open chignolin_tutorial.cxc

# 1. Load the equilibrated starting structure.
open /data/datasets/chimerax-vampnet/chignolin_modal/chignolin/equilibrated.pdb

# 2. Attach the MD trajectory as a coordset on top of it. The bundle's
#    load_ensemble command handles this and adds the ensemble to the
#    session-scoped registry so subsequent commands can see it.
vampnet load_ensemble md /data/datasets/chimerax-vampnet/chignolin_modal/chignolin/replica_0/traj.dcd source md

# 3. Fit the VAMPnet. 2 states is the natural folded/unfolded
#    decomposition for CLN025; lag 100 frames (1 ns at our 10 ps stride)
#    is enough to resolve the slow mode.
vampnet fit nStates 2 lag 100 features ca_distances epochs 80

# 4. Color the structure by state. As you scrub the coordslider, the
#    structure recolors automatically (folded -> blue, unfolded -> orange
#    in the default palette).
vampnet states

# 5. Build the per-state mean structures so you can visually compare
#    folded vs unfolded in the same scene.
vampnet means

# 6. Render the slow mode as a synthetic animated trajectory.
vampnet animate mode 1 nFrames 100

# 7. Surface the MSM transition matrix as a structured graph.
vampnet network

# 8. (Optional) Persist the fitted model so a subsequent ChimeraX session
#    can reload it without retraining.
vampnet save ~/Downloads/chignolin_vampnet.pkl

# 9. (Optional) Start the HTTP/MCP bridge so an external LLM agent can
#    drive future bundle commands programmatically.
vampnet mcp serve port 7345
